#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:107
msgid "getGet()"
msgstr "getGet()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:109
msgid "The ``getGet()`` method will pull from ``$_GET``."
msgstr "The ``getGet()`` method will pull from ``$_GET``."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:111
msgid "``$request->getGet()``"
msgstr "``$request->getGet()``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:114
msgid "getPost()"
msgstr "getPost()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:116
msgid "The ``getPost()`` method will pull from ``$_POST``."
msgstr "The ``getPost()`` method will pull from ``$_POST``."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:118
msgid "``$request->getPost()``"
msgstr "``$request->getPost()``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:121
msgid "getCookie()"
msgstr "getCookie()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:123
msgid "The ``getCookie()`` method will pull from ``$_COOKIE``."
msgstr "The ``getCookie()`` method will pull from ``$_COOKIE``."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:125
msgid "``$request->getCookie()``"
msgstr "``$request->getCookie()``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:128
msgid "getServer()"
msgstr "getServer()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:130
msgid "The ``getServer()`` method will pull from ``$_SERVER``."
msgstr "The ``getServer()`` method will pull from ``$_SERVER``."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:132
msgid "``$request->getServer()``"
msgstr "``$request->getServer()``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:135
msgid "getPostGet()"
msgstr "getPostGet()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:137
msgid ""
"In addition, there are a few utility methods for retrieving information "
"from either ``$_GET`` or ``$_POST``, while maintaining the ability to "
"control the order you look for it:"
msgstr "In addition, there are a few utility methods for retrieving information \"from either ``$_GET`` or ``$_POST``, while maintaining the ability to \"control the order you look for it:"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:140
msgid "``$request->getPostGet()`` - checks ``$_POST`` first, then ``$_GET``"
msgstr "``$request->getPostGet()`` - checks ``$_POST`` first, then ``$_GET``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:143
msgid "getGetPost()"
msgstr "getGetPost()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:145
msgid "``$request->getGetPost()`` - checks ``$_GET`` first, then ``$_POST``"
msgstr "``$request->getGetPost()`` - checks ``$_GET`` first, then ``$_POST``"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:148
msgid "getVar()"
msgstr "getVar()"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:150
#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:364
msgid ""
"This method exists only for backward compatibility. Do not use it in new "
"projects. Even if you are already using it, we recommend that you use "
"another, more appropriate method."
msgstr "This method exists only for backward compatibility. Do not use it in new \"projects. Even if you are already using it, we recommend that you use \"another, more appropriate method."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:154
msgid ""
"The ``getVar()`` method will pull from ``$_REQUEST``, so will return any "
"data from ``$_GET``, ``$_POST``, or ``$_COOKIE`` (depending on php.ini "
"`request-order <https://www.php.net/manual/en/ini.core.php#ini.request-"
"order>`_)."
msgstr "The ``getVar()`` method will pull from ``$_REQUEST``, so will return any \"data from ``$_GET``, ``$_POST``, or ``$_COOKIE`` (depending on php.ini \"`request-order <https://www.php.net/manual/en/ini.core.php#ini.request-\"order>`_)."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:156
msgid ""
"If you want to validate POST data only, don't use ``getVar()``. Newer "
"values override older values. POST values may be overridden by the "
"cookies if they have the same name, and you set \"C\" after \"P\" in "
"`request-order <https://www.php.net/manual/en/ini.core.php#ini.request-"
"order>`_."
msgstr "If you want to validate POST data only, don't use ``getVar()``. Newer \"values override older values. POST values may be overridden by the \"cookies if they have the same name, and you set \\"C\\" after \\"P\\" in \"`request-order <https://www.php.net/manual/en/ini.core.php#ini.request-\"order>`_."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:161
msgid ""
"If the incoming request has a ``Content-Type`` header set to "
"``application/json``, the ``getVar()`` method returns the JSON data "
"instead of ``$_REQUEST`` data."
msgstr "If the incoming request has a ``Content-Type`` header set to \"``application/json``, the ``getVar()`` method returns the JSON data \"instead of ``$_REQUEST`` data."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:167
msgid "Getting JSON Data"
msgstr "JSON 데이터 가져오기"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:169
msgid ""
"You can grab the contents of ``php://input`` as a JSON stream with "
"``getJSON()``."
msgstr "You can grab the contents of ``php://input`` as a JSON stream with \"``getJSON()``."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:171
msgid ""
"This has no way of checking if the incoming data is valid JSON or not, "
"you should only use this method if you know that you're expecting JSON."
msgstr "This has no way of checking if the incoming data is valid JSON or not, \"you should only use this method if you know that you're expecting JSON."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:176
msgid ""
"By default, this will return any objects in the JSON data as objects. If "
"you want that converted to associative arrays, pass in ``true`` as the "
"first parameter."
msgstr "By default, this will return any objects in the JSON data as objects. If \"you want that converted to associative arrays, pass in ``true`` as the \"first parameter."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:179
msgid ""
"The second and third parameters match up to the ``$depth`` and ``$flags``"
" arguments of the `json_decode() <https://www.php.net/manual/en/function"
".json-decode.php>`_ PHP function."
msgstr "The second and third parameters match up to the ``$depth`` and ``$flags``\" arguments of the `json_decode() <https://www.php.net/manual/en/function\".json-decode.php>`_ PHP function."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:183
msgid "Getting Specific Data from JSON"
msgstr "Getting Specific Data from JSON"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:185
msgid ""
"You can get a specific piece of data from a JSON stream by passing a "
"variable name into ``getJsonVar()`` for the data that you want or you can"
" use \"dot\" notation to dig into the JSON to get data that is not on the"
" root level."
msgstr "You can get a specific piece of data from a JSON stream by passing a \"variable name into ``getJsonVar()`` for the data that you want or you can\" use \\"dot\\" notation to dig into the JSON to get data that is not on the\" root level."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:190
msgid ""
"If you want the result to be an associative array instead of an object, "
"you can pass true in the second parameter:"
msgstr "If you want the result to be an associative array instead of an object, \"you can pass true in the second parameter:"

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:195
msgid ""
"See the documentation for :php:func:`dot_array_search()` in the ``Array``"
" helper for more information on \"dot\" notation."
msgstr "See the documentation for :php:func:`dot_array_search()` in the ``Array``\" helper for more information on \\"dot\\" notation."

#: ../../source/incoming/incomingrequest.rst:200
